<PageLayout title="Privacy & cookies" description="How optional analytics and cookie choices work on the DannStarr Electronics website.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 space-y-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Your choice</h2>
    <p>This website works without analytics. Google Analytics 4 is optional and is only loaded after you accept. Rejecting is just as easy as accepting. We remember either choice in this browser’s local storage for up to 180 days. If storage is unavailable, analytics stays off. Clearing browser storage resets your choice.</p>
    <p>Use <button type="button" data-cookie-settings hidden class="underline cursor-pointer">Cookie settings</button> in this page or the footer to change your choice. Rejecting after accepting stops further collection, removes this site’s GA cookies where accessible, and reloads the page to unload Google’s library. It cannot undo information already sent.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Optional Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>When accepted, analytics helps us understand visits to public website pages. It uses cookies called <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_BL5KVVGNMX</code> to distinguish browsers and sessions, with a maximum configured lifetime of 180 days. We do not use this integration for advertising or Google signals.</p>
    <p>We send the public page address and a fixed site title, not the page’s own title or text. Only recognised, fixed marketing source and medium values may appear in the address sent to analytics; arbitrary campaign names, tracking IDs and other query parameters block analytics altogether. Known in-page anchors work normally but are never sent; unknown fragments and unknown pages block analytics. We do not rewrite the address in your browser.</p>
    <p>For recognised search engines, we send only the referring website’s HTTPS origin (such as <code>https://www.google.co.uk</code>), never its path, search terms or other query or fragment data. Other referring addresses are not sent. This helps distinguish organic search visits without collecting search text. This integration does not send form answers, names, contact details, booking details or click destinations. Do not put personal information in website addresses.</p>
    <p>Google receives technical information such as your IP address and browser information when its service is loaded. Google processes analytics data and may process it outside the UK. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="underline" rel="noreferrer">Google’s privacy policy</a>. Withholding consent prevents this website’s analytics integration from contacting Google; we do not send cookieless denied-consent pings.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Other site features</h2>
    <p>The contact page embeds Google Maps, which loads automatically as you approach the map, independently of your analytics choice. Loading the map connects your browser to Google, which receives technical connection information and may use cookies or similar technologies. Rejecting analytics does not block the map. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="underline" rel="noreferrer">Google’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>The site also remembers your light/dark theme locally. Following links to booking, shop or other third-party services takes you to separate services with their own privacy information. This notice covers this website’s optional analytics, not those services.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Questions</h2>
    <p>Contact DannStarr Electronics at <a href="mailto:dannstarrelectronics@gmail.com" class="underline">dannstarrelectronics@gmail.com</a> about this website’s privacy or analytics choices.</p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
